1
00:00:03,052 --> 00:00:03,961
Look at the sky!

2
00:00:04,011 --> 00:00:06,356
Green curtains dancing, without a sound.

3
00:00:06,406 --> 00:00:07,375
No fire, no lamp…

4
00:00:07,425 --> 00:00:09,880
Why does the sky light up near the poles?

5
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:14,192
Mila takes out her compass: the needle points north,

6
00:00:14,242 --> 00:00:15,982
right where the sky glows.

7
00:00:16,032 --> 00:00:16,465
A clue!

8
00:00:16,515 --> 00:00:18,168
Earth is a giant magnet…

9
00:00:18,942 --> 00:00:20,456
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:22,972 --> 00:00:23,559
Mini mode!

11
00:00:23,609 --> 00:00:25,600
The Sun doesn't only give light:

12
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:29,808
it constantly blows billions of tiny electric specks toward Earth.

13
00:00:29,858 --> 00:00:31,261
That's the solar wind.

14
00:00:32,042 --> 00:00:33,540
Luckily, Earth is a giant magnet:

15
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:35,134
its magnetic field forms a shield.

16
00:00:35,184 --> 00:00:38,370
It deflects the specks, and guides some of them toward the two poles,

17
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:39,545
sliding along its lines.

18
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,534
Way up high, a hundred kilometers up,

19
00:00:43,584 --> 00:00:45,116
the specks hit the air.

20
00:00:45,166 --> 00:00:48,073
Oxygen glows green, nitrogen blue and pink,

21
00:00:48,123 --> 00:00:49,242
like a neon sign.

22
00:00:49,292 --> 00:00:50,530
That's the aurora!

23
00:00:51,328 --> 00:00:53,366
And it glows in a ring around both poles:

24
00:00:53,416 --> 00:00:56,371
northern lights in the north, southern lights in the south.

25
00:00:56,421 --> 00:00:57,848
When the Sun blows very hard,

26
00:00:57,898 --> 00:01:00,190
the ring widens and we see them farther away.

27
00:01:00,962 --> 00:01:03,563
That's why the sky lights up near the poles.

28
00:01:04,461 --> 00:01:07,954
Specks from the Sun, guided to the poles by Earth's magnet,

29
00:01:08,004 --> 00:01:09,806
make the air glow way up high.

30
00:01:10,964 --> 00:01:13,804
With an adult: bring a magnet near a compass.

31
00:01:13,854 --> 00:01:14,895
The needle turns!

32
00:01:14,945 --> 00:01:16,179
It feels the magnet,

33
00:01:16,229 --> 00:01:17,963
just as it feels the Earth.

34
00:01:18,741 --> 00:01:20,783
And why does rain have a smell?

35
00:01:20,833 --> 00:01:22,183
The answer tomorrow.
